          "type": "turn",
          "question": "If someone has COPD and an exacerbation, is that one code or two?",
          "answer": "The retrieved guidance says COPD is coded as J44 in ICD-10-CM. Its fourth character records whether a complication is present at that visit. The subdivisions include one for COPD with acute lower respiratory infection and one for COPD with acute exacerbation. The stable form uses the unspecified code. (Source: \"Coding chronic obstructive pulmonary disease: J44 and its two complication codes.\")\n\nThe same source says the two complication codes \"are not alternatives.\" That suggests both can be relevant, but the retrieved text cuts off before it explains how they are applied together or in what order. So I can't tell you from these results whether an exacerbation with a respiratory infection takes both codes, or how they are sequenced.\n\nFor that answer, check the full J44 section of the official ICD-10-CM guidelines or ask a trained medical coder. The coder would work from the clinician's documentation, not from a general explanation.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
